====Exterior====
Climb the stairway and enter the eastern doorway on the lower level.

====1F (East)====
Three of the four cabins here are connected. Visit the isolated northwest cabin to find a [[Harbor Mail]], then go down the stairs in the northeast corner.

====B1F (East)====
Visit the north-central cabin to collect a [[Dive Ball]], and the southwest cabin for an [[Escape Rope]]. Climb up the stairs in the northwest corner.

====1F (West)====
Enter the north cabin to grab a [[Revive]]. Exit the cabin, then use the floormat to the south to reach the exterior of the ship.

====Exterior====
Climb up the upper stairway and enter the Captain's office.

====Captain's office====
There is a Scientist here examining blueprints of the ship, investigating the wreckage on behalf of [[Captain Stern]]. The captain has asked him to find a special Scanner, but he has so far been unsuccessful. Collect the {{ho|Storage Key}} from the southwest corner, then return to the basement level.

====B1F (East)====
Examine the locked door to the northeast cabin to insert the Storage Key. The door opens, but the key becomes stuck in the lock and is left behind. Pick up {{TM|13|Ice Beam}} from inside, then visit the south-central cabin. Seawater has flooded a large part of the room, so use {{m|Dive}} to explore below.

====Underwater====
Swim westward and enter a small room to the north, then use Dive again to surface in an isolated area near the front of the ship.

====B1F (West)====
This area houses six cabins. From left to right, Rooms 1 to 3 are located on the south side, and Rooms 4 to 6 are located on the north side. Rooms 1, 2, 4, and 6 are locked, and debris in Room 5 blocks the doorway.

=====Room 3=====
Begin by visiting Room 3. Immediately upon entering, something sparkling catches your eye; this signifies a hidden item. Examine the northeast corner to find the source: the [[Key to Room 1|Rm. 1 Key]]. Collect the [[Water Stone]] and exit the cabin.

=====Room 1=====
Examine the door to insert the Rm. 1 Key. Like before, the key becomes stuck and remains in the lock. Another sparkling item can be found near the west wall: the [[Key to Room 4|Rm. 4 Key]]. The other sparkling item is only a bit of trash. Pick up {{TM|18|Rain Dance}} from the middle of the room, and exit the cabin.

=====Room 4=====
Three sparkling items can be found here. The two to the east are only trash, but examine the trash can in the northwest corner to find the [[Key to Room 6|Rm. 6 Key]].

=====Room 6=====
Enter the cabin and pick up the [[Luxury Ball]], then follow the narrow hallway to reach the adjoining cabin.

=====Room 5=====
Room 5 holds three sparkling bits of trash, but a fourth item, the [[Key to Room 2|Rm. 2 Key]], lies three steps south of the left-hand trash can.

=====Room 2=====
Visit Room 2 and collect the [[Scanner]] for [[Captain Stern]]'s assistant. Return to the Captain's office and show it to him, and he asks if you would deliver it to Stern in {{DL|Slateport City|Slateport Harbor}} for him, as he must continue his investigation of the ship.

==Slateport City==
===Slateport Harbor===
Visit the harbor building and speak to [[Captain Stern]]. He notices the [[Scanner]] right away and asks if you would trade something for it, as it would be useful for his deep-sea research. He offers the choice between two items: the [[Deep Sea Tooth|DeepSeaTooth]] and [[Deep Sea Scale|DeepSeaScale]].

Both items are associated with {{p|Clamperl}}; the DeepSeaTooth doubles its {{stat|Special Attack}} when held, while the DeepSeaScale does the same for its {{stat|Special Defense}}.

In addition, when held by Clamperl and the Pokémon is [[trade]]d away, each item induces a separate [[Evolution]]. The DeepSeaTooth triggers Clamperl's Evolution into {{p|Huntail}}, while the DeepSeaScale causes it to evolve into {{p|Gorebyss}} instead.
